[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743994751","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-2743994751","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":2743994751,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jjgl_","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-21T17:21:30Z","updated_at":"2025-03-21T17:38:38Z","body":">  I think additive blending can simply be solved by using a fog color of black, while the premul will need black where alpha is 0 and fade toward the color based on the alpha value.\n\nIs there a correct way to fix this for Subtract and Multiply as well? As I understand it, blend modes are implemented on the hardware, so we can't override how they work. All we could do is try to compute fog differently on materials with a blend mode other than Mix to try to compensate for the different blending formula.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743994751/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3863852280","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-3863852280","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":3863852280,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mTbT4","user":{"login":"Arazalera","id":149334681,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOaqmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149334681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera","html_url":"https://github.com/Arazalera","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arazalera/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-07T07:16:01Z","updated_at":"2026-02-07T07:16:01Z","body":"For multiply blending, could it be `fragColor = mix(fragColor,vec3(1.0),fog.a);`? (would need a backdrop of the same/similar color as the fog, which is usually the case for volumetric fog)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3863852280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3895267166","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-3895267166","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":3895267166,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oLQ9e","user":{"login":"jitspoe","id":7751182,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTExODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe","html_url":"https://github.com/jitspoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T07:06:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T07:06:13Z","body":"I think that would probably look close enough but might not technically be correct.  It would definitely look better than doing nothing, but if you think of an extreme case where, say you had a sprite that has a multiply value 0, so it's completely black and it's in front of a wall that is completely red (1, 0, 0).  Not taking fog into account would cause it to be black regardless at any distance.  Now say we had white fog with an alpha of 0.5 `fragColor = mix(fragColor,vec3(1.0),fog.a);` would change that sprite to multiply by 0.5, and the red would start showing through.  Not sure how visible this would be in practice, though.  To solve it for real would mean doing the multiply in a shader with the color buffer, but that's not really viable for multiple layers of transparency.  I think this could be a \"good enough\" solution where most people wouldn't even notice.  Definitely better than just showing sprites unfogged.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3895267166/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5165652290","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-5165652290","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":5165652290,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM-WZQg","user":{"login":"OOPS-ALL-SOLACE","id":1854915,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTQ5MTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1854915?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE","html_url":"https://github.com/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-03T11:19:20Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T11:20:34Z","body":"<img width=\"784\" height=\"722\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5732f57-5c57-461a-b1c2-a95ae03b8737\" />\n\nThis is still the case as of 4.7, The light cones are unshaded Additive blending, only using Vertex colors as tint with a texture on it. Without fog, it looks correct but fog adds into the geometry itself, making it partly visible for some reason... It makes for a really jarring look, but if i disable the fog on the material, the light cones just bleed through the fog. Not exactly the desired look.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5165652290/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5347216881","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-5347216881","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":5347216881,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPrgN8Q","user":{"login":"ibe-denaux","id":70886156,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODg2MTU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70886156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux","html_url":"https://github.com/ibe-denaux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T19:50:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T19:50:26Z","body":"I'm using volumetric fog for light shafts, and this breaks additive effects in a very jarring way. Is there a workaround for additive effects at least?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5347216881/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5347316484","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-5347316484","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":5347316484,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPrmTBA","user":{"login":"ibe-denaux","id":70886156,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODg2MTU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70886156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux","html_url":"https://github.com/ibe-denaux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibe-denaux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T20:00:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T20:00:30Z","body":"I found that there is `render_mode fog_disabled` for custom shaders, and a flag on StandardMaterial3D's. Maybe this could be of use to you too, @OOPS-ALL-SOLACE.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5347316484/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5443480786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-5443480786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":5443480786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRHTs0g","user":{"login":"ueshita","id":1732153,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIxNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1732153?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita","html_url":"https://github.com/ueshita","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:26:01Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:26:01Z","body":"I adjusted the formula for fog blending.\nThis will result in a natural-looking appearance.\n\nCurrent:\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"646\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/60d3270a-99fb-4215-acd9-c470f8d5f072\" />\n\nFog Blending Fixed:\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"646\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d9235eb-d1e4-4aa9-9516-40fae187780d\" />\n\nFor example, in Forward+ Crustered, the code would look like this.\n\n```glsl\n// fog.rgb *= fog.a;\n// fog.a = 1.0 - fog.a;\n#if defined(BLEND_ADD) || defined(BLEND_SUB)\n\tfrag_color.a *= fog.a;\n#elif defined(BLEND_PREMUL_ALPHA)\n\tfrag_color *= fog.a;\n#elif defined(BLEND_MUL)\n\tfrag_color = mix(vec4(1.0), frag_color, fog.a);\n#else\n\tfrag_color.rgb = frag_color.rgb * fog.a + fog.rgb;\n#endif\n```\n\nIf everything looks good, I'll submit the PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5443480786/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5448677208","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-5448677208","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":5448677208,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRMQ3WA","user":{"login":"OOPS-ALL-SOLACE","id":1854915,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTQ5MTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1854915?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE","html_url":"https://github.com/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T05:06:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T05:06:30Z","body":"> I found that there is `render_mode fog_disabled` for custom shaders, and a flag on StandardMaterial3D's. Maybe this could be of use to you too, [@OOPS-ALL-SOLACE](https://github.com/OOPS-ALL-SOLACE).\n\nI did that, but the way I worked around it is to basically turn the albedo color to black the further away you are from the light shaft, essentially giving it a distance fade so the fog doesn't have time to add into it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5448677208/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5535393867","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-5535393867","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":5535393867,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSe9oSw","user":{"login":"jitspoe","id":7751182,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTExODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe","html_url":"https://github.com/jitspoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T03:50:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T03:50:58Z","body":"> For example, in Forward+ Crustered, the code would look like this.\n> \n> // fog.rgb *= fog.a;\n> // fog.a = 1.0 - fog.a;\n> #if defined(BLEND_ADD) || defined(BLEND_SUB)\n> \tfrag_color.a *= fog.a;\n> #elif defined(BLEND_PREMUL_ALPHA)\n> \tfrag_color *= fog.a;\n> #elif defined(BLEND_MUL)\n> \tfrag_color = mix(vec4(1.0), frag_color, fog.a);\n> #else\n> \tfrag_color.rgb = frag_color.rgb * fog.a + fog.rgb;\n> #endif\n> \n> If everything looks good, I'll submit the PR.\n\nAdd, sub, mul, and and mix all look good, but I think you might need to account for the alpha value in prumul alpha or it'll end up looking black when fogged out.  Might need to do both `frag_color *= fog.a;` and `frag_color.a *= fog.a;`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5535393867/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5560539547","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-5560539547","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":5560539547,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABS28Zmw","user":{"login":"ueshita","id":1732153,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIxNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1732153?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita","html_url":"https://github.com/ueshita","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ueshita/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-06T16:21:44Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T16:21:44Z","body":"Thanks for taking a look! There is indeed an issue with fog blending in prumul alpha.\nHowever, `frag_color *= fog.a` already scales both RGB and alpha because `frag_color` is a `vec4`. The suggested additional multiplication would therefore apply fog.a to alpha twice.\n\nTo keep the result consistent with standard mix, I think we should preserve the material's alpha and add the fog contribution weighted by that alpha:\n\n```glsl\n#elif defined(BLEND_PREMUL_ALPHA)\n\tfrag_color.rgb = frag_color.rgb * fog.a + fog.rgb * frag_color.a;\n#else\n\tfrag_color.rgb = frag_color.rgb * fog.a + fog.rgb;\n#endif\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5560539547/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5724214616","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104427#issuecomment-5724214616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104427","id":5724214616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVTCVWA","user":{"login":"jitspoe","id":7751182,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTExODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe","html_url":"https://github.com/jitspoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-18T02:27:04Z","updated_at":"2026-09-18T02:27:04Z","body":"Ah, I had a bit of a brain fart moment there.  Your new code looks correct, though!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5724214616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]